Meta today updated the Muse app for iOS to add Apple Watch support, which means Muse users can access the proactive AI agent from the watch.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/muse-apple-watch-app.jpg" alt="" width="1874" height="1054" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1076651" /><br/>
The app adds the Muse character to the watch with an option to text it, dictate text to it, or call it. There's also a Muse complication for quick access.<br/>
<br/>
Muse is Meta's personal AI agent that can complete tasks for users. It is available as a standalone app and is also built into Instagram, Facebook, and other Meta apps. The yeti-like character Meta designed to represent Muse has become popular, and it is front and center on the Apple Watch.<br/>
<br/>
